startup\n\n5. **internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go**:\n   - `log.Printf()` for cleanup operations\n\n### **3. Entry Points in cmd/**\n\n**cmd/claude-tap/main.go**:\n- **Startup flow**: Parse `--tap-*` flags → detect target → create proxy → start proxy → launch Claude as child process → handle signals → print summary\n- **Key logging points**:\n  - Line 160: `log.Printf(\"upstream target: %s\", target)`\n  - Line 175: `log.Printf(\"proxy listening on %s\", proxyURL)`\n  - Lines 169, 180, 204: Error logging with `log.Fatalf()`\n\n**cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go**:\n- **Backend server startup**: Parse config → create server → start server\n- **Key logging points**:\n  - Line 52: `log.Fatalf(\"create server: %v\", err)`\n  - Line 59: `log.Fatalf(\"server error: %v\", err)`\n\n### **4. Key Files in internal/**\n\n- **internal/proxy/reverse.go**:\n  - Proxy logic with HTTP request interception\n  - SSE streaming support\n  - Turn-based request tracking\n  - Logging patterns: `[Turn N] status message`\n\n- **internal/sse/reassembler.go**:\n  - No logging (pure utility)\n\n- **internal/backend/server.go**:\n  - HTTP server with API handlers\n  - Minimal logging (startup/shutdown)\n\n- **internal/backend/store/sqlite.go**:\n  - No logging (database operations)\n\n- **internal/session/**:\n  - Session management utilities\n  - No logging (metadata handling)\n\n- **internal/config/**:\n  - Client configuration\n  - No logging (pure config)\n\n### **5. Trace Configuration and Paths**\n\n**Command-line Flags for Trace**:\n- `--tap-output-dir DIR` - Override default trace directory\n- If not specified, uses `trace.DefaultTraceDir()`\n\n**Project Detection**:\n1. From git remote origin URL (extracts repo name)\n2. Fallback to current directory name\n\n**Session Trace Initialization**:\n- Via HTTP endpoint `/_internal/trace-init`\n- Receives: session_id, machine_id, project_slug, transcript_path\n- Creates structured trace path with project separation\n\n### **Summary**\n\nThe project has:\n1. **Simple logging**: Uses standard Go `log` with timestamp + microseconds\n2. **Structured trace output**: JSONL format with token usage statistics\n3. **Hierarchical trace paths**: Organized by project and session\n4. **No structured logging library**: Just basic `log.*` calls\n5. **Turn-based proxy logging**: Each request/response gets a turn number for correlation\n\nThe current system is lightweight with minimal logging, focusing on trace recording rather than detailed operational logging."}]}]}
