 package API and implementation\n2. How to initialize the logger in both proxy mode and backend mode\n3. Specific logging points for each key file (what to log at each point)\n4. How to handle the trace directory resolution for both modes\n","subagent_type":"Plan"},"tool_response":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for adding a daily-rotating file logger to the claude_tap_plus Go project.\n\n## Requirements\n1. **Daily log files**: One log file per day, e.g., `.claude-tap-plus/.traces/2026-05-30.log`\n2. **Detailed debug logging**: Function enter/exit, parameter values, intermediate states, 10+ entries per module\n3. **Same directory as trace files**: The log files should go into the same base directory used by `internal/trace/` for JSONL trace output\n4. **Log format**: Include timestamp, level, module/function name, message\n\n## Current Codebase Context\n\n### Trace Output Directory\n- Default: `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` (via `trace.DefaultTraceDir()`)\n- Configurable via `--tap-output-dir` flag\n- The trace path is: `baseDir/{project}/{date}_{time}_{shortID}.jsonl`\n- Log files should go directly in `baseDir/` (e.g., `baseDir/2026-05-30.log`)\n\n### Current Logging\n- Uses standard Go `log` package with `log.SetFlags(log.Ltime | log.Lmicroseconds)` in main.go\n- Only ~15 `log.Printf`/`log.Fatalf` calls across entire codebase\n- No structured logging library\n\n### Project Structure\nKey files to add logging to:\n- `cmd/claude-tap/main.go` - CLI entry, proxy lifecycle, child process management, subcommand routing\n- `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go` - Backend subcommand entry\n- `internal/proxy/reverse.go` - Reverse proxy: request forwarding, header redaction, SSE/non-SSE, turn tracking\n- `internal/sse/reassembler.go` - SSE byte stream reassembler\n- `internal/sse/types.go` - SSE types\n- `internal/trace/writer.go` - JSONL trace writer with token stats\n- `internal/trace/anthropic.go` - Anthropic trace fields\n- `internal/usage/anthropic.go` - Anthropic token fields\n- `internal/usage/normalize.go` - Multi-provider normalization\n- `internal/backend/server.go` - HTTP server setup\n- `internal/backend/config.go` - Backend config\n- `internal/backend/api/router.go` - Route definitions\n- `internal/backend/api/issue_handler.go` - Issue API handlers\n- `internal/backend/api/session_handler.go` - Session API handlers\n- `internal/backend/api/health_handler.go` - Health check handler\n- `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go` - Issue business logic\n- `internal/backend/service/session_service.go` - Session business logic\n- `internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go` - Cleanup service\n- `internal/backend/store/sqlite.go` - SQLite store with WAL mode\n- `internal/backend/store/migrations.go` - DB schema\n- `internal/backend/store/issue_store.go` - Issue store interface + impl\n- `internal/backend/store/store.go` - Store interfaces\n- `internal/backend/domain/` - Entity structs\n- `internal/session/` - Session push/pull/status\n- `internal/config/` - Client config, upstream URL detection\n\n### Design Constraints\n- Keep it simple — no external dependencies for logging, use stdlib\n- The logger should be a new internal package: `internal/logger/`\n- Init the logger early in main.go and backend_cmd.go\n- The logger should support both file output AND console output (dual-write like the shell skills do)\n- Date-based rotation: check date on each write, open new file if date changed\n- Thread-safe (the proxy handles concurrent requests)\n\n### Important: Trace directory for backend mode\nThe backend subcommand also needs logging. The backend uses a different config (`--db` flag for database path). For backend mode, logs should go next to the database file or in a default location.\n\nPlease produce a detailed plan covering:\n1. The logger package API and implementation\n2. How to initialize the logger in both proxy mode and backend mode\n3. Specific logging points for each key file (what to log at each point)\n4. How to handle the trace directory resolution for both modes\n","agentId":"adf92872e68ca987b","agentType":"Plan","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have a complete understanding of the entire codebase. Here is the detailed implementation plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: Daily-Rotating File Logger for claude_tap_plus\n\n### 1. Overview and Architecture\n\nThe plan introduces a new `internal/logger` package that provides a daily-rotating, dual-write (file + console), thread-safe logger using only Go stdlib. The logger is initialized early in both `main.go` (proxy mode) and `backend_cmd.go` (backend mode), and then used across all internal packages via package-level functions to avoid threading a logger instance through every function signature.\n\n### 2. The Logger Package: `internal/logger/`\n\n**File: `claude_tap_plus/internal/logger/logger.go`**\n\nThis is the single file for the entire package. It exposes:\n\n```\npackage logger\n\n// Level represents log severity.\ntype Level int\n\nconst (\n    DEBUG Level = iota\n    INFO\n    WARN\n    ERROR\n)\n\n// Init initializes the global logger.\n//   - dir: directory where daily log files are stored (e.g. $HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/)\n//   - consoleEnabled: if true, also write to stderr (for proxy mode where user sees terminal)\n//   - level: minimum level to log\n//\n// Creates the directory if it does not exist.\n// Opens the current day's log file (named YYYY-MM-DD.log).\nfunc Init(dir string, consoleEnabled bool, level Level) error\n\n// Close flushes and closes the current log file.\nfunc Close() error\n\n// SetLevel changes the minimum log level at runtime.\nfunc SetLevel(level Level)\n\n// Debug logs at DEBUG level.\nfunc Debug(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Debugf logs a formatted message at DEBUG level.\nfunc Debugf(module, format string, args ...any)\n\n// Info logs at INFO level.\nfunc Info(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Infof logs a formatted message at INFO level.\nfunc Infof(module, format string, args ...any)\n\n// Warn logs at WARN level.\nfunc Warn(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Warnf logs a formatted message at WARN level.\nfunc Warnf(module, format string, args ...any)\n\n// Error logs at ERROR level.\nfunc Error(module string, msg string, args ...any)\n\n// Errorf logs a formatted message at ERROR level.\nfunc Errorf(module, format string, args ...any)\n```\n\n**Internal structure (unexported):**\n\n```go\nvar (\n    mu            sync.Mutex\n    file          *os.File\n    dir           string\n    console       bool\n    minLevel      Level = INFO\n    currentDate   string        // \"2006-01-02\" format, tracks rotation\n)\n\nfunc write(level Level, module, format string, args ...any) {\n    if level < minLevel {\n        return\n    }\n    mu.Lock()\n    defer mu.Unlock()\n\n    // Check if date changed; if so, rotate.\n    today := time.Now().Format(\"2006-01-02\")\n    if today != currentDate {\n        rotateFile(today)\n    }\n\n    // Format: 15:04:05.000 [LEVEL] module: message\n    ts := time.Now().Format(\"15:04:05.000\")\n    levelStr := [...]string{\"DEBUG\", \"INFO \", \"WARN \", \"ERROR\"}[level]\n    msg := fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)\n    line := fmt.Sprintf(\"%s [%s] %s: %s\\n\", ts, levelStr, module, msg)\n\n    if file != nil {\n        file.WriteString(line)\n    }\n    if console {\n        // Only INFO and above to console; DEBUG is file-only.\n        if level >= INFO {\n            fmt.Fprint(os.Stderr, line)\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nfunc rotateFile(date string) {\n    if file != nil {\n        file.Close()\n    }\n    path := filepath.Join(dir, date+\".log\")\n    f, err := os.OpenFile(path, os.O_CREATE|os.O_WRONLY|os.O_APPEND, 0o644)\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"logger: failed to open %s: %v\\n\", path, err)\n        return\n    }\n    file = f\n    currentDate = date\n}\n```\n\n**Design decisions:**\n- Package-level functions (not a struct instance) so every package can call `logger.Debug(\"proxy\", ...)` without passing references around. This matches the pattern the codebase already uses with `log.Printf`.\n- `sync.Mutex` protects both the file handle and rotation check. The proxy handles concurrent HTTP requests so thread safety is required.\n- Rotation is lazy: checked on every write, no goroutine or timer needed. This is simpler and sufficient for daily rotation.\n- The log line format is `15:04:05.000 [LEVEL] module: message\\n` -- human-readable, no structured JSON overhead, easy to grep.\n- `console` flag allows dual-write. Proxy mode needs terminal output; backend mode runs as a daemon where stderr may go to /dev/null.\n- `Init(\"\")` with empty dir is a no-op safe mode where writes are silently discarded, preventing nil panics if Init fails.\n\n### 3. Initialization in Both Modes\n\n#### 3a. Proxy Mode (`cmd/claude-tap/main.go`)\n\nIn the `main()` function, immediately after `log.SetFlags(...)`, add logger initialization:\n\n```\nLocation: cmd/claude-tap/main.go, main() function, after log.SetFlags line (line 40)\n\n// Determine log directory: same as trace output dir.\n// At this point tapOutputDir is not yet parsed, so compute default.\nlogDir := trace.DefaultTraceDir()\n// (Later, after flag parsing in runProxy, re-init if user specified --tap-output-dir)\n```\n\nThen in `runProxy()`, after parsing `tapOutputDir` (around line 152):\n\n```\n// Re-initialize logger with the actual output dir.\nif tapOutputDir != \"\" {\n    if err := logger.Init(tapOutputDir, tapVerbose, logger.DEBUG); err != nil {\n        log.Printf(\"warning: logger init failed: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThe `--tap-verbose` flag already exists. When verbose is true, set level to DEBUG and enable console. When false, set level to INFO and disable console (file-only for INFO/WARN/ERROR).\n\nIn `main()`, also add `defer logger.Close()`.\n\nFor subcommands `session-push`, `session-pull`, `session-status`, initialize the logger with a default directory but INFO level and no console (these commands are interactive but do not need debug logging):\n\n```\n// After detecting subcommand (line 42-50 area):\nlogDir := trace.DefaultTraceDir()\nlogger.Init(logDir, false, logger.INFO)\ndefer logger.Close()\n```\n\n#### 3b. Backend Mode (`cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`)\n\nIn `runBackend()`, after parsing args but before creating the server:\n\n```\nLocation: cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go, runBackend() function, after flag parsing loop (around line 47)\n\n// Determine log directory for backend.\n// If DBPath is set, put logs next to the database file.\n// Otherwise use the default trace directory.\nvar logDir string\nif cfg.DBPath != \"\" && cfg.DBPath != \"backend.db\" {\n    logDir = filepath.Dir(cfg.DBPath)\n} else {\n    logDir = trace.DefaultTraceDir()\n}\nif err := logger.Init(logDir, false, logger.DEBUG); err != nil {\n    log.Printf(\"warning: logger init failed: %v\", err)\n}\ndefer logger.Close()\n```\n\nBackend mode does not need console output (it is a long-running server), so `consoleEnabled = false`. The level is DEBUG because the backend is the component most in need of diagnostics.\n\n### 4. Specific Logging Points Per Key File\n\nBelow I list every file that should receive logging calls, organized by module, with the exact function/location, level, module string, and what to log.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.1 `cmd/claude-tap/main.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"main\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `main()`, after arg parsing | INFO | `\"subcommand: %s\"` or `\"mode: proxy\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after target detection | DEBUG | `\"detected upstream target: %s\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after proxy start | INFO | `\"proxy started on port %d\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after ResolveCmd | DEBUG | `\"claude binary resolved to: %s\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after building child env | DEBUG | `\"child env ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=%s\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after cmd.Start | INFO | `\"claude child process started, pid=%d\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, signal handler, first signal | INFO | `\"received signal %v, forwarding to child\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, signal handler, second signal | WARN | `\"received second signal %v, killing child\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, after cmd.Wait | INFO | `\"claude process exited: %v\"` |\n| `runProxy()`, summary print | INFO | `\"summary: api_calls=%v input=%v output=%v\"` |\n| `runSessionPush()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"session-push: all=%v force=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `runSessionPull()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"session-pull: all=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `runSessionStatus()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"session-status: verbose=%v\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.2 `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"backend.cmd\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `runBackend()`, entry | INFO | `\"backend starting: host=%s port=%d db=%s\"` |\n| `runBackend()`, after logger init | DEBUG | `\"logger initialized: dir=%s\"` |\n| `runBackend()`, after NewServer | DEBUG | `\"server created successfully\"` |\n| `runBackend()`, after srv.Start | INFO | `\"backend server started\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.3 `internal/proxy/reverse.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"proxy\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewReverseProxy()` | DEBUG | `\"new proxy: target=%s baseDir=%s\"` |\n| `Start()` | INFO | `\"proxy listening on %s:%d\"` |\n| `Stop()` | INFO | `\"proxy stopping\"` |\n| `serveHTTP()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"request: %s %s\"` (method + path) |\n| `serveHTTP()`, after body read | DEBUG | `\"request body size: %d bytes\"` |\n| `serveHTTP()`, after building upstream URL | DEBUG | `\"upstream URL: %s\"` |\n| `serveHTTP()`, after upstream request | DEBUG | `\"upstream response: status=%d\"` |\n| `handleStreaming()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"streaming response: status=%d\"` |\n| `handleStreaming()`, after reassembler | DEBUG | `\"SSE events collected: %d\"` |\n| `handleStreaming()`, after trace write | DEBUG | `\"trace written for turn %d\"` |\n| `handleNonStreaming()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"non-streaming response: status=%d\"` |\n| `handleNonStreaming()`, decompression | DEBUG | `\"decompressed response: %d -> %d bytes\"` |\n| `handleTraceInit()`, entry | INFO | `\"trace-init: session=%s machine=%s slug=%s\"` |\n| `handleTraceInit()`, after writer created | INFO | `\"trace file created: %s\"` |\n| `handleTraceInit()`, fallback closed | DEBUG | `\"fallback writer closed\"` |\n| `getWriter()`, fallback path | WARN | `\"no session writer, using fallback: %s\"` |\n\nReplace existing `log.Printf` calls with the corresponding `logger.Xxx` calls. The existing calls in this file are:\n\n| Current call | Replacement |\n|---|---|\n| `log.Printf(\"proxy server error: %v\", err)` | `logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"server error: %v\", err)` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] upstream error: %v\", ...)` | `logger.Warn(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] upstream error: %v\", ...)` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] trace write error: %v\", ...)` | `logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] trace write error: %v\", ...)` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] <- %d stream done ...\")` | `logger.Info(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] <- %d stream done ...\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"[Turn %d] <- %d (%dms ...)\")` | `logger.Info(\"proxy\", \"[Turn %d] <- %d (%dms ...)\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"trace-init: failed ...\")` | `logger.Error(\"proxy\", \"trace-init: failed ...\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"trace initialized: %s\")` | `logger.Info(\"proxy\", \"trace initialized: %s\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"fallback trace: %v\")` | `logger.Warn(\"proxy\", \"fallback trace: %v\")` |\n| `log.Printf(\"using fallback trace: %s\")` | `logger.Warn(\"proxy\", \"using fallback trace: %s\")` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.4 `internal/sse/reassembler.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"sse\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `FeedBytes()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"FeedBytes: chunk size=%d, buf total=%d\"` |\n| `feedLine()`, event dispatched | DEBUG | `\"SSE event: type=%s data_len=%d\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, message_start | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: message_start, model=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, message_delta | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: message_delta, stop_reason=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, content_block_start | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: content_block_start idx=%d type=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, content_block_delta | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: content_block_delta idx=%d delta_type=%v\"` |\n| `accumulate()`, content_block_stop | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: content_block_stop idx=%d\"` |\n| `accumulateChatCompletionChunk()`, first chunk | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: chat chunk init, model=%s\"` |\n| `accumulateChatCompletionChunk()`, finish | DEBUG | `\"accumulate: chat chunk finish_reason=%v\"` |\n\nNote: SSE events can be very frequent during streaming. These DEBUG logs will only fire when `--tap-verbose` is true, so they will not impact normal performance.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.5 `internal/trace/writer.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"trace\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewTraceWriter()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"creating trace writer: path=%s\"` |\n| `NewTraceWriter()`, after mkdir | DEBUG | `\"ensured directory: %s\"` |\n| `NewTraceWriter()`, success | INFO | `\"trace writer opened: %s\"` |\n| `Write()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"writing record #%d\"` |\n| `Write()`, after marshal | DEBUG | `\"record marshaled: %d bytes\"` |\n| `Write()`, error | ERROR | `\"write record failed: %v\"` |\n| `Close()` | INFO | `\"trace writer closed: %d records written\"` |\n| `DefaultTraceDir()` | DEBUG | `\"default trace dir: %s\"` |\n| `DetectProjectName()` | DEBUG | `\"detected project name: %s\"` |\n| `NewTracePath()` | DEBUG | `\"trace path: %s\"` |\n| `NewSessionTracePath()` | DEBUG | `\"session trace path: %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.6 `internal/trace/anthropic.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"trace.anthropic\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NewAnthropicTraceRecord()` | DEBUG | `\"new trace record: turn=%d method=%s path=%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.7 `internal/usage/normalize.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"usage\