ssage |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Health()` | DEBUG | `\"health check\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.19 `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"svc.issue\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Check()` | DEBUG | `\"check: repo=%s numbers=%v\"` |\n| `Claim()` | DEBUG | `\"claim: repo=%s #%d session=%s\"` |\n| `UpdateStatus()` | DEBUG | `\"update status: repo=%s #%d -> %s\"` |\n| `Release()` | DEBUG | `\"release: repo=%s #%d\"` |\n| `ReleaseSession()` | DEBUG | `\"release session: %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.20 `internal/backend/service/session_service.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"svc.session\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Register()` | DEBUG | `\"register: %s slug=%s\"` |\n| `Close()` | DEBUG | `\"close: %s reason=%s\"` |\n| `List()` | DEBUG | `\"list: filter=%+v\"` |\n| `Get()` | DEBUG | `\"get: %s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.21 `internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"svc.cleanup\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `CleanupTimedOutSessions()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"starting timed-out session cleanup\"` |\n| `CleanupTimedOutSessions()`, result | INFO | `\"cleaned up %d timed-out sessions\"` |\n| `CleanupTimedOutSessions()`, error | ERROR | `\"cleanup failed: %v\"` |\n\nReplace existing `log.Printf(\"cleanup timed-out sessions: %v\", err)` with `logger.Error(...)`.\nReplace existing `log.Printf(\"cleaned up %d timed-out sessions\", n)` with `logger.Info(...)`.\n\n---\n\n#### 4.22 `internal/session/collect.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"session.push\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SessionPush()`, entry | INFO | `\"session-push: all=%v force=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `pushAllProjects()`, scanning | DEBUG | `\"scanning projects dir: %s\"` |\n| `pushSingleProject()`, info | DEBUG | `\"push: project=%s slug=%s claude_dir=%s\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"collect: slug=%s dir=%s\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, each file | DEBUG | `\"session file: %s size=%d\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, skip | DEBUG | `\"skip existing: %s\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, copy | INFO | `\"copied: %s (%d bytes)\"` |\n| `collectProject()`, meta saved | DEBUG | `\"meta.json updated: %d sessions\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.23 `internal/session/restore.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"session.pull\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SessionPull()`, entry | INFO | `\"session-pull: all=%v dry_run=%v\"` |\n| `pullAllProjects()`, scanning | DEBUG | `\"scanning: %s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, entry | DEBUG | `\"restore: slug=%s target=%s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, each file | DEBUG | `\"restore file: %s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, skip | DEBUG | `\"skip existing: %s\"` |\n| `restoreProject()`, restored | INFO | `\"restored: %s -> %s\"` |\n| `updateClaudeJSON()`, update | INFO | `\"updated .claude.json: lastSession=%s\"` |\n\n---\n\n#### 4.24 `internal/session/status.go`\n\n**Module string:** `\"session.status\"`\n\n| Location | Level | Message |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SessionStatus()`, entry | INFO | `\"session-status: storage=%s\"` |\n| `SessionStatus()`, each project | DEBUG | `\"project: %s slug=%s local=%d claude=%d\"` |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Trace Directory Resolution Summary\n\n| Mode | Log Directory | How Resolved |\n|---|---|---|\n| Proxy (default) | `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` | `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` |\n| Proxy (`--tap-output-dir DIR`) | `DIR` | User-provided flag value |\n| Backend (default DB) | `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` | `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` (same as proxy default) |\n| Backend (`--db PATH`) | `filepath.Dir(PATH)` | Next to the database file |\n| Session subcommands | `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces/` | `trace.DefaultTraceDir()` |\n\nThe resulting log file path for today would be: `{logDir}/2026-05-30.log`\n\n### 6. Implementation Sequence\n\n**Step 1: Create `internal/logger/logger.go`**\n- Write the full package as described in section 2.\n- This is the only new file. Zero external dependencies.\n\n**Step 2: Add `\"github.com/liaohch3/claude-tap/claude_tap_plus/internal/logger\"` import to `cmd/claude-tap/main.go`**\n- Add `logger.Init()` call in `main()` with default trace dir.\n- Add `defer logger.Close()`.\n- Add re-init in `runProxy()` with actual tapOutputDir.\n- Add init in each subcommand runner.\n\n**Step 3: Add import and init to `cmd/claude-tap/backend_cmd.go`**\n- Add logger init after flag parsing, before server creation.\n- Add `defer logger.Close()`.\n\n**Step 4: Update `internal/proxy/reverse.go`**\n- Add import.\n- Replace all 15 `log.Printf` calls with `logger.Xxx` calls.\n- Add new debug logging points at each function entry/exit.\n\n**Step 5: Update `internal/trace/writer.go`**\n- Add import.\n- Add debug/info logging at each function entry.\n- Keep the existing `log.Printf` calls in `main.go` that use Go's stdlib `log` -- those are for early startup before logger is available.\n\n**Step 6: Update remaining packages in order:**\n- `internal/backend/server.go` -- replace `log.Printf` with logger calls\n- `internal/backend/service/cleanup_service.go` -- replace `log.Printf`\n- `internal/backend/store/sqlite.go`\n- `internal/backend/store/migrations.go`\n- `internal/backend/store/issue_store.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/router.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/issue_handler.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/session_handler.go`\n- `internal/backend/api/health_handler.go`\n- `internal/backend/service/issue_service.go`\n- `internal/backend/service/session_service.go`\n- `internal/config/client.go`\n- `internal/config/claudeconfig.go`\n- `internal/session/collect.go`\n- `internal/session/restore.go`\n- `internal/session/status.go`\n- `internal/sse/reassembler.go`\n- `internal/usage/normalize.go`\n- `internal/trace/anthropic.go`\n\n**Step 7: Remove `log.SetFlags` line from `main.go` (optional)**\n- Once all `log.Printf` calls are migrated to `logger`, the stdlib `log` package is no longer needed in most files. However, keeping `log.Fatalf` in entry points (`main.go`, `backend_cmd.go`) is fine since those are fatal exits.\n\n**Step 8: Test**\n- Run `go build ./...` to verify compilation.\n- Run existing tests (`go test ./...`) to verify no regressions.\n- Manually verify log file creation in the trace directory.\n- Verify daily rotation by temporarily changing the date check logic or waiting until midnight.\n\n### 7. Potential Challenges and Mitigations\n\n**Challenge 1: Import cycles.** The `logger` package must not import any other internal package. It is a leaf dependency. The plan ensures this -- `logger.go` only imports stdlib (`sync`, `os`, `fmt`, `time`, `path/filepath`).\n\n**Challenge 2: Performance.** The mutex lock on every log write could theoretically contend under high concurrency. Mitigation: the lock is brief (format + write), and Go's `os.File.Write` with append mode is already atomic for small writes on most OSes. For this project's traffic volume (local proxy for one user), this is not a concern.\n\n**Challenge 3: File descriptor leaks on rotation.** The `rotateFile` function closes the old file before opening the new one. If the open fails, `file` becomes nil and subsequent writes silently skip file output (console still works). This is acceptable degradation.\n\n**Challenge 4: Logging during tests.** Tests should not create log files. Add a `func InitForTest()` that sets `minLevel` to a high value (or a `func Discard()` that disables output), or simply let tests not call `Init` at all (all writes are silently discarded when `file == nil`).\n\n### 8. Count of Logging Points\n\nPer the detailed tables above:\n- `main.go`: 13 entries\n- `backend_cmd.go`: 4 entries\n- `reverse.go`: 19 entries (including replacements)\n- `reassembler.go`: 9 entries\n- `writer.go`: 11 entries\n- `anthropic.go`: 1 entry\n- `normalize.go`: 2 entries\n- `client.go`: 5 entries\n- `claudeconfig.go`: 3 entries\n- `server.go`: 7 entries\n- `config.go` (backend): 1 entry\n- `sqlite.go`: 6 entries\n- `migrations.go`: 3 entries\n- `issue_stor