id **does NOT change** after `/clear`\n- According to issue #3046, the same session_id is maintained\n- This allows hooks and other features to reference the same session\n\n## Transcript File Behavior\n\n### What Happens to the Transcript File\n- **The transcript file is NOT deleted** when `/clear` is used\n- It continues to exist at: `~/.claude/projects/<project>/<session-id>.jsonl`\n- The file contains the complete conversation history, including messages before `/clear`\n\n### Transcript File Issues\nThere's a known issue (issue #3046) where:\n- After `/clear`, some Stop hooks may receive a transcript path that points to a file\n- But the file might be missing or inaccessible for context extraction\n- This causes hooks to fall back to generic messages instead of contextual responses\n- The issue is related to how transcript file paths are handled after clearing\n\n## Session Management Commands\n\n### Related Commands:\n- **`/resume`** - Switch to a different conversation\n- **`/branch`** - Create a fork from the current conversation\n- **`/compact`** - Replace history with a summary\n- **`/context`** - Show what's currently consuming context\n\n### Session Persistence:\n- Sessions are stored per project directory\n- Sessions are automatically saved as you work\n- Sessions remain accessible for resuming after `/clear`\n- Transcript files are removed after 30 days by default (configurable)\n\n## Key Takeaways\n\n1. **Context Reset, Not Session Reset**: `/clear` only clears the conversation context, not the entire session\n2. **Same Session ID**: The session_id remains the same after `/clear`\n3. **Transcript Preservation**: The transcript file continues to exist with the full conversation history\n4. **Resume Capability**: You can resume conversations that were cleared using `/resume`\n5. **Known Issue**: There's a bug where transcript file paths may become inaccessible after `/clear` for some hooks\n\n## When to Use `/clear`\n- When you need to reset context between unrelated tasks\n- If you've corrected Claude more than twice on similar issues\n- To free up context space in long-running sessions\n- To start fresh while keeping the session available for resuming later\n\nSources:\n- [Claude Code Docs - Sessions](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sessions)\n- [GitHub Issue #3046](https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/3046)"}]}]}
