[2026-05-30 16:48:45] [INFO] [SubagentStop] Input: {"session_id":"85b4b220-e119-417e-b974-e5edde848812","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\85b4b220-e119-417e-b974-e5edde848812.jsonl","cwd":"D:\\CodeDevelopment\\CodeProject\\claude-hk","permission_mode":"plan","agent_id":"af4cb3bbcea4facdf","agent_type":"Explore","hook_event_name":"SubagentStop","stop_hook_active":false,"agent_transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\Administrator\\.claude\\projects\\D--CodeDevelopment-CodeProject-claude-hk\\85b4b220-e119-417e-b974-e5edde848812\\subagents\\agent-af4cb3bbcea4facdf.jsonl","last_assistant_message":"## Summary of Key Package Interfaces and Patterns\n\nBased on my exploration of the claude_tap_plus project, here's a comprehensive understanding of the key packages:\n\n### 1. **Logger Package** (`internal/logger/`)\n\n**Key Interface:**\n```go\nfunc Init(dir string, consoleEnabled bool, level Level) error\n```\n\n**Parameters:**\n- `dir`: Log file directory (creates automatically if needed)\n- `consoleEnabled`: Boolean - whether to also output to stderr (only for INFO+ level)\n- `level`: Minimum log level (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARN`, `ERROR`)\n\n**Log Levels:**\n```go\nconst (\n    DEBUG Level = iota // DEBUG level\n    INFO               // INFO level  \n    WARN               // WARN level\n    ERROR              // ERROR level\n)\n```\n\n**Dual-Write Mechanism:**\n- File logging: Writes to `YYYY-MM-DD.log` in the specified directory with format `15:04:05.000 [LEVEL] module: message`\n- Console logging: When `consoleEnabled=true`, logs INFO and above to stderr\n- Automatic date rotation: Checks for new days and rotates logs\n- Thread-safe with mutex protection\n\n**Usage Example:**\n```go\nlogger.Init(\"/path/to/logs\", true, logger.DEBUG)\ndefer logger.Close()\nlogger.Info(\"proxy\", \"started on :8080\")\nlogger.Debug(\"store\", \"query: %s\", sql)\n```\n\n### 2. **Config Package** (`internal/config/`)\n\n**Core Functions:**\n\n**`DetectTarget(cfg *ClientConfig) string`** - Determines upstream API URL with priority:\n1. Environment variable (e.g., `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`)\n2. `~/.claude.json` config file\n3. Default target address\n\n**`ClaudeClient`** - Pre-configured for Claude Code:\n```go\nvar ClaudeClient = ClientConfig{\n    Cmd:              \"claude\",\n    BaseURLEnv:       \"ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL\", \n    DefaultTarget:    \"https://api.anthropic.com\",\n    NestingEnvKeys:   []string{\"CLAUDECODE\", \"CLAUDE_CODE_SSE_PORT\"},\n    InjectSettingsEnv: true,\n}\n```\n\n**`ResolveCmd(cfg *ClientConfig) (string, error)`** - Finds binary in PATH\n\n**`BuildChildEnv(cfg *ClientConfig, proxyURL string) []string`** - Creates subprocess environment:\n- Inherits current environment\n- Sets base URL to point to local proxy\n- Clears nesting-related env vars to prevent recursion\n\n**Profile/Config Reading:**\n- Reads `~/.claude.json` for `base_url` and `env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL`\n- JSON format with nested env section\n- Silently ignores format errors\n\n### 3. **Trace Package** (`internal/trace/`)\n\n**`DefaultTraceDir() string`** - Returns default trace directory:\n- Windows: `$HOME/.claude-tap-plus/.traces`\n- Fallback: `.claude-tap-plus/.traces`\n\n**Trace Writer Implementation:**\n```go\ntype TraceWriter struct {\n    mu           sync.Mutex\n    file         *os.File\n    writer       *bufio.Writer\n    count        int\n    inputTokens  int64\n    outputTokens int64\n    cacheRead    int64\n    cacheCreate  int64\n    modelsUsed   map[string]int\n}\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- JSON Lines format (one JSON object per line)\n- Automatic token counting and model usage tracking\n- Thread-safe concurrent writes\n- Project-based organization with git repo detection\n- Machine ID and session ID support\n- Automatic directory creation\n\n**`Summary() map[string]any`** Returns:\n```go\n{\n    \"api_calls\":           int,\n    \"input_tokens\":        int64,\n    \"output_tokens\":       int64, \n    \"cache_read_tokens\":   int64,\n    \"cache_create_tokens\": int64,\n    \"models_used\":         map[string]int\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Proxy Package** (`internal/proxy/`)\n\n**`NewReverseProxy(target, traceDir string) *ReverseProxy`** - Creates proxy instance:\n- `target`: Upstream API base URL\n- `traceDir`: Base directory for trace files\n\n**Key Implementation Details:**\n```go\ntype ReverseProxy struct {\n    target    string\n    baseDir   string\n    writer    *trace.TraceWriter\n    fallbackW *trace.TraceWriter\n    client    *http.Client\n    turn      atomic.Int64\n    server    *http.Server\n    startOnce sync.Once\n}\n```\n\n**`Summary() map[string]any`** - Returns aggregated trace statistics from current trace writer\n\n**Core Workflow:**\n1. Internal endpoints handling (`/_internal/`)\n2. Path whitelist checking\n3. Request body reading\n4. Upstream request forwarding\n5. Stream/non-stream response handling\n6. Trace recording with session ID extraction\n\n**Stream Processing:**\n- SSE reassembler for handling chunked responses\n- Real-time forwarding to client\n- Event reconstruction for tracing\n\n**Key Patterns Observed:**\n1. **Configuration First**: All packages use configuration-driven approach with sensible defaults\n2. **Graceful Degradation**: Logger handles init failures, proxy has fallback trace writer\n3. **Concurrency Safety**: All packages use mutex/atomic for thread safety\n4. **JSON Lines Format**: Trace uses JSONL for efficient streaming and parsing\n5. **Project Organization**: Automatic git repo detection for trace organization\n6. **Environment Isolation**: Careful environment variable management for subprocess isolation","background_tasks":[],"session_crons":[]}
